    "The threshold": {
      "act": "I - before the surface",
      "truth": "pick a number and call it the skin. iso = 0.5 is a DECISION, not a discovery: move it and the object changes while the field stays exactly the same.",
      "tiers": {
        "small": [],
        "medium": [],
        "large": [],
        "applied": []
      },
      "count": 0,
      "thin": true
    },
    "The sample grid": {
      "act": "II - asking",
      "truth": "you cannot ask every point, so you ask a lattice. Resolution is a budget, and every isosurface you have ever seen was an interview with finitely many places.",
      "tiers": {
        "small": [],
        "medium": [],
        "large": [],
        "applied": []
      },
      "count": 0,
      "thin": true
    },
    "The fifteen cases": {
      "act": "II - asking",
      "truth": "eight corners, each in or out: 256 configurations, 15 after symmetry. The lookup table is the whole algorithm - the rest is bookkeeping.",
      "tiers": {
